        "## 2. Numbering one sequence three ways\n",
        "\n",
        "A **numbering scheme** assigns a position label to every residue in a variable domain, so that\n",
        "\"position 52\" means the structurally equivalent place in *any* antibody. That is the whole purpose:\n",
        "antibodies differ in length, so raw sequential counting is useless for comparison.\n",
        "\n",
        "The three you must know:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Scheme | Basis | Still used because |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| **Kabat** (1970s) | sequence variability | enormous legacy literature, many patents |\n",
        "| **Chothia** | structural loop positions | canonical CDR conformations are defined on it |\n",
        "| **IMGT** | germline gene alignment | current standard; databases and most modern tools use it |\n",
        "\n",
        "They are *different conventions over the same molecule.* None is wrong. They disagree.\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's number the same VH under each and just look at the length of the result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 21,
      "id": "6c9d9230",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6c9d9230",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "a494c805-a6c2-429c-d243-2be38b97e774"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "imgt      chain=H  120 residues numbered, highest position = 128\n",
            "kabat     chain=H  120 residues numbered, highest position = 113\n",
            "chothia   chain=H  120 residues numbered, highest position = 113\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "for scheme in [\"imgt\", \"kabat\", \"chothia\"]:\n",
        "    numbering, chain_type = number(VH, scheme=scheme)\n",
        "    occupied = [(p, a) for (p, ic), a in numbering if a != \"-\"]\n",
        "    highest = max(p for (p, ic), a in numbering if a != \"-\")\n",
        "    print(f\"{scheme:<9} chain={chain_type}  {len(occupied)} residues numbered, \"\n",
        "          f\"highest position = {highest}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "2b792dc6",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2b792dc6"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Read that carefully.** The same 119 amino acids. IMGT runs the position counter up to 128,\n",
        "Kabat and Chothia stop at 113.\n",
        "\n",
        "The schemes are not just re-labelling — they reserve *different numbers of slots*. IMGT allocates\n",
        "fixed positions for structural elements whether or not a given antibody fills them, so most antibodies\n",
        "have gaps. Kabat numbers what is there and uses insertion codes when it runs out of room.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is why you cannot convert between schemes with arithmetic. There is no offset to add."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "91d902fe",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "91d902fe"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. The H52 problem\n",
        "\n",
        "Now, Let's ask each scheme what amino acid sits at **heavy chain position 52**,\n",
        "and at position 33."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 22,
      "id": "409a6d5b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "409a6d5b",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "b414124e-c643-4b2c-ccbc-a5f1a4a6b48e"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "scheme    H33     H52     H100\n",
            "----------------------------------\n",
            "imgt      None    W       A       \n",
            "kabat     Y       Y       F       \n",
            "chothia   Y       Y       F       \n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def residue_at(seq, scheme, position):\n",
        "    \"\"\"What amino acid is at this position under this scheme? None if the slot is empty.\"\"\"\n",
        "    numbering, _ = number(seq, scheme=scheme)\n",
        "    for (p, insertion_code), aa in numbering:\n",
        "        if p == position and insertion_code == \" \" and aa != \"-\":\n",
        "            return aa\n",
        "    return None\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"{'scheme':<10}{'H33':<8}{'H52':<8}{'H100'}\")\n",
        "print(\"-\" * 34)\n",
        "for scheme in [\"imgt\", \"kabat\", \"chothia\"]:\n",
        "    row = [residue_at(VH, scheme, p) for p in (33, 52, 100)]\n",
        "    print(f\"{scheme:<10}\" + \"\".join(f\"{str(r):<8}\" for r in row))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c9852510",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c9852510"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Sit with this for a second.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **H52 is tryptophan under IMGT and tyrosine under Kabat and Chothia.** Same molecule, same position\n",
        "  label, different amino acid.\n",
        "- **H33 does not exist under IMGT** — that slot is empty in this antibody — but it is a tyrosine under\n",
        "  Kabat and Chothia.\n",
        "\n",
        "So the answer to today's question is **no**. \"Mutate H52\" is ambiguous unless the scheme is stated.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is not a pedantic edge case. It is a routine cause of real errors: a mutation ordered against\n",
        "the wrong residue, a literature position mapped onto the wrong structure, a dataset merged from two\n",
        "sources that used different conventions. **Whenever you record an antibody position, record the scheme\n",
        "with it.**"
      ]
    },
